# What EAS Build does not need uploaded.
#
# The first build shipped a 592 MB archive and spent twenty minutes uploading
# it, almost all of which was `node_modules` — 456 MB that the build server
# installs for itself from package.json and the lockfile.
#
# It is already in .gitignore. EAS did not honour that, because this project
# is a subdirectory of a git repository whose root is one level up: the
# archiver only applies the ignore rules it finds at the project root, and
# there is no .gitignore there. `.easignore` is the documented way to say it
# explicitly, and when present it is what EAS reads instead.
#
# Rule of thumb for anything added here later: exclude it if the build server
# can regenerate it, and keep it if the build reads it.

# Installed on the builder from package-lock.json.
node_modules/

# Local caches and build output.
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo
expo-env.d.ts

# Generated by prebuild on the builder itself.
/ios
/android
.kotlin/

# Scratch directories from headless-browser verification runs.
.smoke/
.exportcheck/
.expo-export-check/
.claude/

# Secrets never belong in a build archive. Build-time configuration goes in
# eas.json under the profile's `env`, which is where EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is.
.env
.env.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.pem

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.orig.*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
